    <!--
    Rust workspace source set.  Built with Cargo, not by this manifest.

    The fifteen C translation units above remain the authoritative description of
    the retained reference implementation, and they are what this manifest builds.
    They are read and never edited: they are the algorithmic oracle that the
    memory-safe Rust reimplementation of this library is developed and
    differentially tested against.  The Rust crates below carry no source, depend
    or include-file entry of their own, deliberately: a .rs path offered to a
    consumer of this manifest would be offered to a C compiler.

    Workspace root:

      Cargo.toml           virtual manifest: members, shared package metadata,
                           workspace lints, release profile
      Cargo.lock           committed, because this workspace ships a system library
      rust-toolchain.toml  toolchain channel, with rustfmt and clippy
      .rustfmt.toml        formatting policy
      clippy.toml          lint thresholds
      deny.toml            cargo deny license and advisory policy
      cbindgen.toml        C header generation, diffed against zlib.h
      rust/README.md       developer guide for the port

    crates/zlib-rs         The safe core.  Carries forbid(unsafe_code) with no_std
                           plus alloc and an empty dependencies table, so it pulls
                           in no third party crate at all.  Every algorithm lives
                           here.
                           subtrees:   adler32/  crc32/  deflate/  trees/
                                       inflate/ (inftrees and inffast folded in)
                                       gz/
                           top level:  lib.rs  allocate.rs  error.rs  config.rs
                                       read_buf.rs  weak_slice.rs  infback.rs
                                       compress.rs  uncompress.rs

    crates/libz-rs-sys     The C ABI facade, and the only crate permitted to write
                           unsafe.  [lib] name = "z" with
                           crate-type = ["cdylib", "staticlib", "rlib"] makes Cargo
                           emit libz.so and libz.a from one definition of the
                           exported surface.  build.rs drives the packaging, and
                           csrc/ holds the two C translation units stable Rust
                           cannot declare: the variadic gzprintf and gzvprintf, and
                           the codetype prototype of inflate_table.

    crates/zlib-rs-differential
                           Dev-only oracle harness.  Its build script compiles the
                           C units above into a test-only archive, so both
                           implementations are co-resident in one test process and
                           comparing them is a memory compare.  It appears in the
                           dependencies table of neither shipped crate, which is
                           what keeps reference zlib an oracle rather than a build
                           dependency.

    fuzz/                  Dev-only cargo fuzz targets; its own workspace, excluded
                           from the root one.
    benches/               Dev-only criterion benchmark suites.

    Packaging is unaffected.  Both implementations emit the same library named by
    dlname above, install the same two public headers, and export the same ABI
    under the same zlib.map version script: libz.so.1.3.2.1-motley with SONAME
    libz.so.1, the libz.so.1 and libz.so symlinks onto it, and libz.a.  A consumer
    includes zlib.h and links -lz either way, unrecompiled.

    Entry points, spelled without the leading dashes their cargo and make options
    need, because an XML comment may not hold two consecutive hyphens.  README,
    rust/README.md and Makefile.in carry the exact command lines:

      cargo build      release profile, packages zlib-rs and libz-rs-sys
      cargo build      release profile, package libz-rs-sys, features libz-compat
      cargo test       release profile, whole workspace
      make rust        stage the installable shared and static drop-in libraries
      make rust-test   link and run the unmodified C drivers against them
      make rust-header regenerate the cbindgen header and diff it against zlib.h
      make rust-clean  remove the Cargo target directory and the staged artifacts
      cmake            configure with the ZLIB_BUILD_RUST option for the same
                       drop-in through CMake
    -->
</package>

